title: The Social Welfare Review
subtitle: Coalition government turns every safety net into a question of deservingness.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and ministry_count >= 1 and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_social_welfare_review_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_social_welfare_review_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/cards/workers-public-services.webp

= The Social Welfare Review

Inflation has shifted the value of every threshold while local offices carry
caseloads designed for a different decade. No single ministry owns the whole
failure, which means the cabinet can either coordinate it or continue passing
the file around.

[? if left_is_junior_partner = 1: **[+ coalition_senior_partner +] holds the
premiership** and the Finance Ministry reads every indexation clause twice.
Objection risk on a contested measure: **[+ coalition_objection_risk +]%**.?]

- @social_floor
- @working_poor
- @protect_services
- @target_exposure

@social_floor
title: Establish a cabinet-wide social floor
subtitle: Cost: 2 budget capacity. Index support and make access portable — the clause Finance most wants deleted.
choose-if: budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Indexation and a common access floor require two budget points.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 2;
const objectionRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const objected =
    Q.left_is_junior_partner &&
    objectionRoll * 100 < Number(Q.coalition_objection_risk) * 1.05;
Q.last_card_objection = objected ? 1 : 0;
Q.last_card_objector = Q.coalition_senior_partner;
if (objected) {
    Q.household_security += 2;
    Q.government_delivery += 1;
    Q.pensioner_support += 1;
    Q.left_coalition_dissent += 6;
    Q.coalition_blur += 3;
    Q.household_policy_pressure += 4;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
    Q.ministry_overruled_count += 1;
    Q.ministry_overruled_last = "Indexed social floor";
    Q.government_goal_welfare = 1;
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.coalition_senior_partner +
        " strikes automatic indexation out of the social floor";
} else {
    Q.household_security += 6;
    Q.workers_support += 4;
    Q.pensioner_support += 3;
    Q.health_capacity += 2;
    Q.government_delivery += 4;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 3;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.household_policy_pressure =
        Math.max(0, Q.household_policy_pressure - 10);
    Q.government_goal_welfare = 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The cabinet adopts an indexed social floor across benefits and services";
}
!}

Thresholds update automatically and people no longer lose support merely by
crossing an administrative boundary. The reform is expensive precisely
because years of frozen values made deterioration look free.

[? if last_card_objection = 1: What reaches the cabinet minutes is a one-off
adjustment and a commitment to review indexation in the next medium-term
framework. Every threshold will therefore be worth less again next year, on
schedule.?]

- #poland_card_finish


@working_poor
title: Extend the child and care benefits to the working poor
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Take the material claim PiS built its majority on and complete it.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Extending eligibility requires one budget point.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
const objectionRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const objected =
    Q.left_is_junior_partner &&
    objectionRoll * 100 < Number(Q.coalition_objection_risk) * 0.9;
Q.last_card_objection = objected ? 1 : 0;
Q.last_card_objector = Q.coalition_senior_partner;
Q.government_goal_welfare = Math.max(
    1,
    Number(Q.government_goal_welfare) || 0
);
if (objected) {
    Q.household_security += 1;
    Q.left_coalition_dissent += 5;
    Q.coalition_blur += 2;
    Q.household_policy_pressure += 3;
    Q.ministry_overruled_count += 1;
    Q.ministry_overruled_last = "Working-poor benefit extension";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.coalition_senior_partner +
        " defers the benefit extension to the next budget";
} else {
    Q.household_security += 5;
    Q.workers_support += 4;
    Q.women_support += 3;
    Q.provincial_welfare_left_affinity += 4;
    Q.industrial_logistics_left_affinity += 3;
    Q.older_welfare_households_left_affinity += 2;
    Q.government_delivery += 3;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 1;
    Q.pis_poll_momentum -= 0.3;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum -= 0.1;
    Q.social_spending_salience += 3;
    Q.household_policy_pressure =
        Math.max(0, Q.household_policy_pressure - 8);
    if (Q.government_party == "pis") {
        Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
        Q.pis_relation -= 4;
    } else {
        Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 3;
    }
    Q.news_headline =
        "Child and care benefits reach the working households they excluded";
}
!}

**Result:** [+ news_headline +].

[? if last_card_objection = 0: The gap PiS never closed was never about
generosity: it was the households just above a threshold, in work, paying full
market prices for care and receiving nothing. They are the exact households that
voted for the 500+ programme and then discovered it was not for them.?][? if
last_card_objection = 1: The extension is deferred to the next budget with warm
words about the direction of travel. The households above the threshold read the
direction of travel on their next invoice.?]

[? if last_card_objection = 0: Completing somebody else's flagship is a strange
way to win an argument, and it is the version of that argument they cannot
answer.?]

- #poland_card_finish


@protect_services
title: Protect local services inside the current settlement
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Keep the institutions alive before expanding entitlements.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Stabilising local service capacity requires one budget point.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; household_security += 3; public_sector_support += 4; health_capacity += 2; government_delivery += 3; fiscal_stress += 1; psl_relation += 2; government_goal_welfare = 1; news_headline = "The welfare review protects local offices, clinics and care services"

The cabinet funds staffing, access and casework while leaving national rates
largely unchanged. It is an institutional defence rather than a new promise,
and rural partners can point to offices that remain open.

- #poland_card_finish


@target_exposure
title: Retarget the existing envelope at the most exposed households
subtitle: Free fallback. Triage inside a fixed envelope: somebody who was receiving support stops.
on-arrival: household_security += 2; pensioner_support += 2; public_trust += 1; government_delivery += 1; progressive_credibility -= 1; progressives_dissent += 3; household_policy_pressure += 3; workers_support -= 1; labor_dissent += 2; government_goal_welfare = 1; last_card_objection = 0; news_headline = "The welfare review redirects existing support toward the most exposed households"

Officials adjust thresholds and case priorities without enlarging the
envelope. The worst cliffs soften. The system remains too small, and nobody in
the room is permitted to mistake triage for a settlement.

- #poland_card_finish
